Conclusions
Our aim in this paper has been to contribute to a growing body of research on trust in automated vehicles and to provide insights into its conceptualization, measurement, and implications. In line with a vast body of literature, trust needs to be discussed at a level of complexity that agrees with its dynamic and multi-layered nature: it develops and changes over time. Yet, the terminology used to describe this dynamic process is often ambiguous and lacks clarity. We therefore present a concise framework based on previous work (see Figure 1) and provide a use-case example demonstrating its application.
In the framework (see Figure 1), the development of an appropriate level of dynamic learned trust is represented as a cycle

